// The input ends in the middle of a token. The automaton walks to the end of the input without ever reaching an
// accepting state, so there is no match to fall back to and the whole remainder is one error. This is the case where a
// scanner which looks one byte past the last one it consumed reads out of bounds, so the trace pins that the error ends
// at the end of the input and not one byte behind it.
//
// The parser is not what this case is about, so the grammar is the single empty production the file format requires.

@scanner {
    ABCD: "abcd";
}

@parser {
    tokens
        : @empty
        ;
}
